<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
    <IncludeBuildOutput>false</IncludeBuildOutput>
    <SuppressDependenciesWhenPacking>true</SuppressDependenciesWhenPacking>
    <DevelopmentDependency>true</DevelopmentDependency>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>false</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <!-- Packaging host only: it contains no compiled output of its own. -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);NU5128</NoWarn>

    <!-- NuGet Package Info -->
    <PackageId>CancelCop.Analyzer</PackageId>
    <!-- Fallback for local packs; the publish workflow overrides this with -p:Version from
             the release tag so the published package always matches the tag. -->
    <Version>1.32.0</Version>
    <Authors>George Wall</Authors>
    <Title>CancelCop.Analyzer — CancellationToken and async/await Roslyn analyzer for C#/.NET</Title>
    <Description>Compile-time CancellationToken and async/await Roslyn analyzer for C#/.NET: catches missing cancellation propagation, ignored ASP.NET Core RequestAborted, EF Core, HttpClient, gRPC, SignalR, and MediatR cancellation, timeout CTS that drops a parent token, sync-over-async deadlocks, blocking I/O, async void, and resource-lifetime bugs across 31 diagnostics—with code fixes. Failures surface in the editor and CI, not only at runtime.</Description>
    <PackageTags>roslyn;roslyn-analyzer;analyzers;analyzer;codefix;code-fix;static-analysis;codeanalysis;csharp;dotnet;cancellation;cancellationtoken;async;async-await;sync-over-async;deadlock;async-void;aspnetcore;RequestAborted;BackgroundService;efcore;httpclient;grpc;signalr;mediatr;WithCancellation;OperationCanceledException;blocking</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Adds CC031: flags blocking synchronization primitives — ManualResetEventSlim.Wait, CountdownEvent.Wait, WaitHandle.WaitOne/WaitAll/WaitAny, Monitor.Wait, Thread.Join — inside async code. These park a thread-pool thread until another thread signals, consuming a pooled thread the awaited continuations may themselves need, and observe no CancellationToken; blocking on cancellationToken.WaitHandle is a common instance. Analyzer-only by design: these primitives have no async counterpart, so the resolution is a design change (SemaphoreSlim.WaitAsync, a TaskCompletionSource, or awaiting the task instead of joining the thread). 31 diagnostics.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/georgepwall1991/CancelCop.Analyzer</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/georgepwall1991/CancelCop.Analyzer</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>

    <!-- Pack both the analyzer and code-fix assemblies into analyzers/dotnet/cs. -->
    <TargetsForTfmSpecificContentInPackage>$(TargetsForTfmSpecificContentInPackage);AddAnalyzerAssembliesToPackage</TargetsForTfmSpecificContentInPackage>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Build-order + bundling references; do not flow as compile/runtime dependencies. -->
    <ProjectReference
      Include="..\CancelCop.Analyzer\CancelCop.Analyzer.csproj"
      PrivateAssets="all"
      ReferenceOutputAssembly="false"
    />
    <ProjectReference
      Include="..\CancelCop.Analyzer.CodeFixes\CancelCop.Analyzer.CodeFixes.csproj"
      PrivateAssets="all"
      ReferenceOutputAssembly="false"
    />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\CancelCop.Analyzer\icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\assets\**\*" Pack="true" PackagePath="assets\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <Target Name="AddAnalyzerAssembliesToPackage">
    <ItemGroup>
      <TfmSpecificPackageFile
        Include="..\CancelCop.Analyzer\bin\$(Configuration)\netstandard2.0\CancelCop.Analyzer.dll"
        PackagePath="analyzers/dotnet/cs"
      />
      <TfmSpecificPackageFile
        Include="..\CancelCop.Analyzer.CodeFixes\bin\$(Configuration)\netstandard2.0\CancelCop.Analyzer.CodeFixes.dll"
        PackagePath="analyzers/dotnet/cs"
      />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>
</Project>
